.TH APT\-TRANSPORT\-CURL\-CHECK 8 "2026-11-17" "apt-transport-curl 0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
apt\-transport\-curl\-check \- print the state of the installation of apt-transport-curl
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apt\-transport\-curl\-check
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run it as root when
.B apt\-get update
or the Application Manager cannot use an
.B https://
repository. It changes nothing and prints no account data. The result is a list of lines marked
.B [ ok ]
or
.BR [FAIL] ,
and a final
.B RESULT:
line that can be pasted into a bug report.
.PP
The script checks the three packages (apt-transport-curl, curl, apt-transport-https), the method files
.RB ( https
should be our script of about 5 kB,
.B https.distrib
the original of about 25 kB), the handshake with apt, a test download over TLS, the clock, free memory, and the last lines of the error log of the method.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/apt\-transport\-curl/check.sh
the script itself.
.TP
.I /tmp/apt\-transport\-curl.errors
the error log of the method.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt\-transport\-curl (8),
.BR n900 (7)
.SH AUTHOR
elPytel. Project: https://github.com/n900-resurrection/apt-transport-curl
